alls", "Prediction markets price Luna around 74-76% to win", "Gray's strong fundraising and heavy outside spending against Luna keep it competitive"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a modest Republican edge: a +6 GOP district partially offset by a strong Democratic national environment and incumbent drag, yielding a small R margin consistent with the late polling average and the Lean R expert consensus. Prediction markets and Luna's Trump endorsement reinforce her as the favorite, though Gray's fundraising and Democratic outside spending make this closer than a typical R+6 seat.", "watch": "A late surge in Democratic turnout or fresh polling showing Gray ahead would move this to a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Anna Paulina Luna (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican incumbent Anna Paulina Luna seeks reelection in a St. Petersburg-area district that leans Republican by about six points, facing Democratic veteran Leela Gray in what both parties treat as a priority race. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the contest Lean R, with two outlets rating it a Tossup, and prediction markets give Luna roughly a three-in-four chance of winning.\n\nThe race is genuinely competitive. Gray has outraised Luna in the most recent reporting period and Democratic-aligned outside groups have spent heavily against the incumbent, while late polls show a narrow race within the margin of error. Still, the district's partisan lean, Luna's incumbency and Trump endorsement, and the national environment only partially offsetting that lean give the Republican the edge heading into election day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.257, "margin": -3.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3197, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2842, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3186, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2913, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -3